<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>Country Coverage</h2>

<div id="A3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Table <a href="#A3.T4" title="Table 4 ‣ Appendix C Country Coverage ‣ EvalMORAAL: Interpretable Chain-of-Thought and LLM-as-Judge Evaluation for Moral Alignment in Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a> provides a breakdown of country representation across the WVS and PEW surveys. The 30 overlapping countries allow for direct cross-dataset validation. The 25 WVS<span id="A3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">-</span>only countries increase coverage in areas underrepresented in the PEW Spring 2013 survey, particularly Sub<span id="A3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text">-</span>Saharan Africa, Central Asia, and Eastern Europe. The 9 PEW-only countries provide additional Middle Eastern and North African representation.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A3.T4" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 4: </span>Country coverage breakdown across WVS and PEW surveys.</figcaption>
